**Considering selection logic**

I’m looking at the selection logic for H2 when it’s in a collapsed H1 range. It appears that if H2 is selected using `selectByBlockId('h2')`, it doesn’t get displayed. I need to expand the ancestors first! So, I should modify `WenzOutlineController.selectByBlockId` to call `expandToRevealBlockId(blockId)` before actually setting the selection. This way, H2 becomes visible when I try to select it. That makes sense to me!
**Analyzing anchor navigation**

I’m focusing on items that handle h2 headers without expanding them unless they target hidden content. Using `selectByAnchor` could be relevant here, but I wonder if block attributes should apply only to outline item anchors. It seems the `WenzRichTextController` has a method to set block anchors, but there isn’t a general way for anchor navigation. So, I’ll think about whether to just use `rg.selectByAnchor` in this context.
